<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis de Carvajal y de la Cueva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1539–<a href="/years/1590">1590</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis de Carvajal y de la Cueva was a Portuguese-born Spanish conquistador and governor who in 1579 received a royal grant to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of León in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>. He began settling it in 1582, founding early settlements in the area of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monterrey">Monterrey</a>. After members of his family were accused of secretly practising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, he was arrested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> and died in prison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-de-carvajal-y-de-la-cueva.jpg" alt="Luis de Carvajal y de la Cueva" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo DelaG · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luis_Carvajal_y_de_la_Cueva.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
